1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,375
Start in 2010, with house prices in Germany, Portugal and Italy on the same line.

2
00:00:06,775 --> 00:00:12,475
Germany climbs steadily. Portugal dips at first, then takes off. Italy slides.

3
00:00:13,675 --> 00:00:20,250
By 2019, the average Italian home is worth 17 percent less than in 2010.

4
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:23,950
Then prices start rising almost everywhere.

5
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:33,132
By 2025, German house prices are up 82 percent on 2010. Portugal's, 146 percent.

6
00:00:33,132 --> 00:00:36,125
Italy's? Still down 2 percent.

7
00:00:36,525 --> 00:00:41,648
Fifteen years, and an Italian home is worth a little less than when it started,

8
00:00:41,648 --> 00:00:42,750
before inflation.

9
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:48,025
Where prices exploded instead: our full video on 28 November.
